{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "unitId": "chapter-curiosity-before-certainty-parts-part-2-exploring-systems-chapter-5-debugging-the-world",
  "generationHash": "sha256:efef6622b30c710b819915fddcf955f2010a945a56c085581ff6e79785e25bc4",
  "granularity": "segment-only",
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "s0001",
      "text": "Chapter 5 — Debugging the World",
      "startMs": 0.0,
      "endMs": 3042.0,
      "charStart": 0,
      "charEnd": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "text": "When people imagine software development, they often picture writing clean, elegant code.",
      "startMs": 3854.0,
      "endMs": 9404.0,
      "charStart": 33,
      "charEnd": 122
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "text": "In practice, a lot of the craft is debugging.",
      "startMs": 10100.0,
      "endMs": 13177.0,
      "charStart": 123,
      "charEnd": 168
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "text": "Things break, often for reasons that are hard to spot at first, and the work is to trace the break back to its source.",
      "startMs": 13177.0,
      "endMs": 20085.0,
      "charStart": 168,
      "charEnd": 286
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "text": "I used to hate debugging because it felt like proof that I had made a mistake.",
      "startMs": 20874.0,
      "endMs": 25135.0,
      "charStart": 289,
      "charEnd": 367
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "text": "Over time, I came to value it for the opposite reason.",
      "startMs": 25646.0,
      "endMs": 28955.0,
      "charStart": 368,
      "charEnd": 422
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "text": "Debugging is one of the fastest ways to understand a system deeply.",
      "startMs": 28955.0,
      "endMs": 33111.0,
      "charStart": 422,
      "charEnd": 489
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "text": "Failure exposes connections that success can hide.",
      "startMs": 33111.0,
      "endMs": 36676.0,
      "charStart": 489,
      "charEnd": 539
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "text": "A feature that works often tells you little about architecture.",
      "startMs": 37128.0,
      "endMs": 40530.0,
      "charStart": 543,
      "charEnd": 606
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "text": "A feature that fails under load, fails only on one browser, or fails only with one kind of user data forces you to ask better questions.",
      "startMs": 40530.0,
      "endMs": 48750.0,
      "charStart": 606,
      "charEnd": 742
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "text": "Where does state live?",
      "startMs": 48750.0,
      "endMs": 50225.0,
      "charStart": 742,
      "charEnd": 764
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "text": "What assumptions are implicit?",
      "startMs": 50712.0,
      "endMs": 52396.0,
      "charStart": 767,
      "charEnd": 797
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "text": "Which components depend on timing?",
      "startMs": 52570.0,
      "endMs": 54648.0,
      "charStart": 798,
      "charEnd": 832
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "text": "The first explanation is usually too simple.",
      "startMs": 55345.0,
      "endMs": 58212.0,
      "charStart": 834,
      "charEnd": 878
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "text": "\"The API is down.\" \"The frontend is broken.\" \"The user did something wrong.\" These guesses are rarely fully false, but they are rarely complete.",
      "startMs": 58212.0,
      "endMs": 68163.0,
      "charStart": 878,
      "charEnd": 1022
    },
    {
      "id": "s0016",
      "text": "Complex failures often span several layers at once.",
      "startMs": 68163.0,
      "endMs": 71483.0,
      "charStart": 1022,
      "charEnd": 1073
    },
    {
      "id": "s0017",
      "text": "Good debugging starts with small, testable steps.",
      "startMs": 72052.0,
      "endMs": 75500.0,
      "charStart": 1077,
      "charEnd": 1126
    },
    {
      "id": "s0018",
      "text": "Reproduce the issue.",
      "startMs": 75709.0,
      "endMs": 77033.0,
      "charStart": 1127,
      "charEnd": 1147
    },
    {
      "id": "s0019",
      "text": "Change one variable.",
      "startMs": 77207.0,
      "endMs": 78670.0,
      "charStart": 1148,
      "charEnd": 1168
    },
    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "text": "Observe the result.",
      "startMs": 78995.0,
      "endMs": 80260.0,
      "charStart": 1169,
      "charEnd": 1188
    },
    {
      "id": "s0021",
      "text": "Add instrumentation.",
      "startMs": 80469.0,
      "endMs": 82048.0,
      "charStart": 1189,
      "charEnd": 1209
    },
    {
      "id": "s0022",
      "text": "Narrow the surface area.",
      "startMs": 82048.0,
      "endMs": 83894.0,
      "charStart": 1209,
      "charEnd": 1233
    },
    {
      "id": "s0023",
      "text": "Compare a failing case to a working one.",
      "startMs": 84230.0,
      "endMs": 86750.0,
      "charStart": 1235,
      "charEnd": 1275
    },
    {
      "id": "s0024",
      "text": "Each step turns confusion into evidence.",
      "startMs": 86750.0,
      "endMs": 89791.0,
      "charStart": 1275,
      "charEnd": 1315
    },
    {
      "id": "s0025",
      "text": "This approach travels well beyond software.",
      "startMs": 90105.0,
      "endMs": 92880.0,
      "charStart": 1318,
      "charEnd": 1361
    },
    {
      "id": "s0026",
      "text": "In organizations, recurring miscommunication is a bug worth tracing.",
      "startMs": 92880.0,
      "endMs": 97431.0,
      "charStart": 1361,
      "charEnd": 1429
    },
    {
      "id": "s0027",
      "text": "In personal routines, repeated friction is a bug worth tracing.",
      "startMs": 97431.0,
      "endMs": 102203.0,
      "charStart": 1429,
      "charEnd": 1492
    },
    {
      "id": "s0028",
      "text": "In policy and process, predictable failure points are bugs worth tracing.",
      "startMs": 102203.0,
      "endMs": 107508.0,
      "charStart": 1492,
      "charEnd": 1565
    },
    {
      "id": "s0029",
      "text": "The specifics change, but the curiosity posture is the same.",
      "startMs": 107508.0,
      "endMs": 111920.0,
      "charStart": 1565,
      "charEnd": 1625
    },
    {
      "id": "s0030",
      "text": "The practical lesson is simple: breakdown is more than inconvenience.",
      "startMs": 112814.0,
      "endMs": 117609.0,
      "charStart": 1631,
      "charEnd": 1700
    },
    {
      "id": "s0031",
      "text": "It is information.",
      "startMs": 117609.0,
      "endMs": 119118.0,
      "charStart": 1700,
      "charEnd": 1718
    },
    {
      "id": "s0032",
      "text": "When a system fails, it reveals where its structure is brittle, where assumptions are outdated, and where small repairs can create disproportionate gains.",
      "startMs": 119118.0,
      "endMs": 128104.0,
      "charStart": 1718,
      "charEnd": 1872
    },
    {
      "id": "s0033",
      "text": "Curiosity treats failure as useful data.",
      "startMs": 128871.0,
      "endMs": 131936.0,
      "charStart": 1876,
      "charEnd": 1916
    },
    {
      "id": "s0034",
      "text": "Once you learn to debug one kind of system, you begin seeing the method everywhere.",
      "startMs": 131936.0,
      "endMs": 136893.0,
      "charStart": 1916,
      "charEnd": 1999
    },
    {
      "id": "s0035",
      "text": "From here, we turn that insight into low-risk action: small experiments",
      "startMs": 137288.0,
      "endMs": 141886.0,
      "charStart": 2002,
      "charEnd": 2073
    },
    {
      "id": "s0036",
      "text": "that trade certainty for faster learning.",
      "startMs": 141944.0,
      "endMs": 144475.0,
      "charStart": 2074,
      "charEnd": 2115
    }
  ]
}
